-- The if-flip of observeContinuousEqualsLetfree: `if Normal == 0.5 then 1
-- else 2` spelled with its condition negated and its arms swapped. The
-- IfThenElse rule derives the False weight as the complement of the True
-- weight, and the complement of `not (Normal == 0.5)`'s mass 1 is the mass 0:
-- the equality's density convention was lost and p(Right 1) answered
-- impossible. A negated condition now swaps the arms instead (task
-- null-set-conventions-not-preserved-under-negation), so every row matches
-- the un-negated spelling's.
main = observe (if not (Normal == 0.5) then 2 else 1) (\v -> v < 2)
